{
 "section_summary": "This section records sentences from the April 1948 Kobe–Osaka riots and a detailed Army review of the principal Kobe trial. Other documents address Tanzan Ishibashi’s purge, restrictions on demonstrations, Japanese party politics, labor policy, and the occupation’s response to communism. Correspondence from Count Makino and a conversation with former Chinese premier Chang Chun offer views on Japan’s political future.",
