   "title": "United States of America vs. Kim Dai Sam et al.: Review of the Staff Judge Advocate",
   "doc_type": "military legal review",
   "start_page": 226,
   "end_page": 237,
   "continues_previous": false,
   "date": "1948-07-07",
   "from": "Marion H. Shoak, Assistant Staff Judge Advocate; Staff Judge Advocate",
   "to": "Commanding General, Eighth Army",
   "about": "Reviews the Kobe military commission trial of eight Koreans and one Japanese after the April riot.",
   "summary": "The review recounts the seizure of the Hyogo governor’s office, pressure to rescind Korean school closures, detention of officials, destruction of communications, and confrontation with U.S. military police. It finds the commission properly constituted and the convictions legally supported, while noting procedural questions and the acquittals of Kim Ko Hong and Cha Yong Seok. The assistant judge advocate recommends halving most sentences as excessive for the proven violence; the staff judge advocate rejects clemency and urges approval of the original sentences.",
